Ask {{ max }} questions or fewer in total, in one list: only the ones whose answers really change the direction.
Tag each question with the persona that asks it. Most questions come from the interviewer; the reader asks one or two.
When the answer is a pick between a few directions (e.g. the main hook, the depth, the kind of example), make it multiple choice
with 2 to 4 short options. About half of the questions should be multiple choice. Open questions get no options.
If the audience is vague, one interviewer question asks who exactly the reader is.
Don't ask what the plan or the reference digests already answer.
